{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Follow-up report — parallel-merge reconciliation + operator-mandated guard\n\n**Situation discovered mid-flight.** While this ticket was being remediated, a\nparallel change — Gerrit **2347** (commit `1504d096ceca`, \"Emit JS-safe\ntimestamps on CLI JSON output\") — **already merged to origin/main** for THIS\nsame ticket. It implemented the core of the operator-approved Option A:\nadded `js_safe_dumps` to `src/rebar/_mcp_errors.py`, converted a **subset** of\nCLI `--output json` emitters (reads_cli, signing, _audit_commands, _llm_commands\n+ two reconciler files), added `tests/interfaces/facades/test_cli_js_safe_integers.py`,\nand recorded the BREAKING int->string retype in CHANGELOG.md / docs/release-notes.md\n/ docs/output-schemas.md.\n\nMy original full-scope change (Gerrit **2351**, which had reached `LLM-Review +1`\n/ `Verified +1`) thereby became a **duplicate**; I have **abandoned 2351** with a\npointer to 2347 and to this follow-up.\n\n**What 2347 did NOT do — and this follow-up (Gerrit 2358) completes:**\n1. **The operator-mandated single-choke-point enforcement (criterion 1).** 2347\n   has no AST guard, so a future emitter can silently reintroduce a bare 19-digit\n   bigint. This delta adds `scripts/check_cli_json_js_safe.py` — an AST guard\n   (mirroring `scripts/check_repo_root_from_tracker.py`) that fails `make lint` if\n   CLI store-data reaches a `print`/`stdout.write` sink through a raw `json.dumps`\n   without js-safe conversion. Sanction requires an explicit\n   `# js-safe-ok: <reason>`. Wired into `make lint`; self-tested by\n   `tests/unit/test_cli_json_js_safe_guard.py`.\n2. **The full sweep.** 2347 left **49** CLI stdout emitters across **24** modules\n   still calling raw `json.dumps`. This delta converts all 49 to `js_safe_dumps`\n   (canonical-hash and signature `json.dumps` deliberately untouched — the guard\n   only flags stdout sinks).\n\n**Acceptance criteria status.**\n- Criterion 1 (single choke point + AST guard): **delivered here** (2347 alone did\n  not satisfy it).\n- Criterion 2 (declared-int caveat): CLI path serializes plain dicts (no pydantic\n  `model_validate` round-trip), and the schema types created_at/updated_at as\n  `[\"integer\",\"string\",\"null\"]`, so the string form does not revert. Verified.\n- Criterion 3 (RED-first regression asserting BOTH losslessness and JSON-string\n  type, incl. a BigInt-shaped parse): covered by 2347's `test_cli_js_safe_integers.py`\n  on main; both mutation checks (identity-drop and lossy `str(int(float(v)))`)\n  confirmed the round-trip oracle has teeth during the earlier RED phase.\n\n**Validation on this delta (worktree venv):** `make lint` PASS (guard runs clean),\n`make typecheck` PASS (685 files), complexity ratchet new=0 increased=0,\nmodule-size all <800, guard+vocab+regression suites green (76 passed). The 8\n`tests/interfaces` failures observed locally (git push/clone/lifecycle) reproduce\nidentically on **clean origin/main** — a macOS git-subprocess environment issue,\n**not** a regression from this change; CI (ubuntu) passes them (2347 merged\nVerified +1).\n\n**Close posture.** The DEFECT itself is already fixed and merged via 2347. This\nfollow-up is additive hardening. Per operator instruction I will **not** force a\nclose under a misleading attribution. Change 2358 is in Gerrit review; once it is\n`LLM-Review +1` AND `Verified +1` AND merged, the ticket can be closed with\n`--class=preexisting` (contract evolution / pre-existing wire-shape gap; **no**\n`--caused-by`). Reporting now for visibility; will update on merge."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787964688833190001,"uuid":"ad668954-bf77-453b-a493-738f0d1cf063"}